    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "{\"unit_id\": \"Harweben\", \"choices\": [], \"reasoning\": \"C1 Hr-jb-Nj.t is made of three words: the god Horus (Hr), jb 'heart', and the goddess Neith (Nj.t), rendered 'Her-ib-Neith'. On consonants alone record 1 could be forced onto it. Har = Hr, w for weak j, b, n, then j dropped and the feminine t omitted. Read as a modern spelling, though, Harweben renders Hr-wbn, 'Horus shines'. That uses the verb wbn 'to shine', with no word 'heart' and no goddess Neith. Record 1 therefore renders different words, so C1 is a different name.\"}"
     }
